      "content": "okay, i see what you're saying about the statutory framework, but i'm still not totally convinced. it feels like you're basically telling me that the privilege side is just \"theoretical idealism\" while mine is the \"practical\" one. \n\nif i'm being honest, it feels like you're sidestepping the actual constitutional question. if the Constitution doesn't explicitly define the limits of executive privilege, shouldn't the default position be that the President has broad discretion to protect the executive branch's integrity? isn't it a bit reductive to frame any broad claim of privilege as just \"bad-faith\" or \"abuse\"?",
